": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L30"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q7_explain_the_procedure_for_minimizing_a_boolean_function_using_a_four_variable_karnaugh_map_state_the_rules_that_must_be_followed_while_forming_groups", "label": "Q7. Explain the procedure for minimizing a Boolean function using a four-variable Karnaugh map. State the rules that must be followed while forming groups.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L35"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q8_minimize_the_following_function_using_a_four_variable_k_map_f_a_b_c_d_\u03c3_0_1_2_3_8_9_10_11", "label": "Q8. Minimize the following function using a four-variable K-map: F(A,B,C,D) = \u03a3(0,1,2,3,8,9,10,11).", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L40"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q9_minimize_f_a_b_c_d_\u03c3_1_3_5_7_9_11_13_15_using_a_k_map_explain_your_grouping", "label": "Q9. Minimize F(A,B,C,D) = \u03a3(1,3,5,7,9,11,13,15) using a K-map. Explain your grouping.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L45"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q10_minimize_f_a_b_c_d_\u03c3_0_2_8_10_11_14_15_using_a_four_variable_k_map", "label": "Q10. Minimize F(A,B,C,D) = \u03a3(0,2,8,10,11,14,15) using a four-variable K-map.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L50"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q11_what_are_don_t_care_conditions_explain_how_they_help_in_k_map_minimization", "label": "Q11. What are don't-care conditions? Explain how they help in K-map minimization.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L55"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q12_a_seven_segment_display_receives_a_4_bit_input_representing_decimal_digits_0_9_inputs_10_15_are_never_used_explain_how_these_unused_inputs_can_be_exploited_during_k_map_minimization", "label": "Q12. A seven-segment display receives a 4-bit input representing decimal digits 0\u20139. Inputs 10\u201315 are never used. Explain how these unused inputs can be exploited during K-map minimization.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L60"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q13_why_is_the_minimal_k_map_expression_not_necessarily_unique_explain_with_reference_to_prime_implicants", "label": "Q13. Why is the minimal K-map expression not necessarily unique? Explain with reference to prime implicants.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L65"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q14_explain_the_operation_of_a_2_1_multiplexer_derive_its_boolean_equation_and_explain_its_truth_table", "label": "Q14. Explain the operation of a 2:1 multiplexer. Derive its Boolean equation and explain its truth table.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L70"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q15_explain_how_a_4_1_multiplexer_can_be_constructed_using_2_1_multiplexers_determine_the_number_of_2_1_multiplexers_required", "label": "Q15. Explain how a 4:1 multiplexer can be constructed using 2:1 multiplexers. Determine the number of 2:1 multiplexers required.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L75"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q16_a_processor_needs_to_select_one_of_eight_possible_data_sources_determine_the_type_of_multiplexer_required_and_the_number_of_select_lines_needed_explain_your_answer", "label": "Q16. A processor needs to select one of eight possible data sources. Determine the type of multiplexer required and the number of select lines needed. Explain your answer.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L80"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q17_implement_f_a_b_c_\u03c3_1_2_5_7_using_an_8_1_multiplexer", "label": "Q17. Implement F(A,B,C) = \u03a3(1,2,5,7) using an 8:1 multiplexer.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L85"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q18_explain_the_operation_of_a_decoder_how_is_a_decoder_different_from_a_multiplexer", "label": "Q18. Explain the operation of a decoder. How is a decoder different from a multiplexer?", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L90"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q19_a_memory_system_contains_eight_memory_modules_a_3_bit_address_is_used_to_select_exactly_one_module_at_a_time_explain_how_a_decoder_can_be_used_for_module_selection", "label": "Q19. A memory system contains eight memory modules. A 3-bit address is used to select exactly one module at a time. Explain how a decoder can be used for module selection.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L95"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q20_differentiate_between_combinational_and_sequential_logic_explain_the_role_of_memory_state_in_sequential_circuits", "label": "Q20. Differentiate between combinational and sequential logic. Explain the role of memory/state in sequential circuits.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L100"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q21_given_the_input_waveforms_of_an_sr_latch_explain_how_the_output_q_is_determined_discuss_the_set_reset_and_hold_conditions", "label": "Q21. Given the input waveforms of an SR latch, explain how the output Q is determined. Discuss the SET, RESET and HOLD conditions.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L105"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q22_a_d_latch_is_transparent_when_clk_1_if_d_during_a_high_clock_period_is_0_1_0_1_explain_the_output_sequence_what_happens_when_the_clock_becomes_low", "label": "Q22. A D latch is transparent when CLK=1. If D during a HIGH clock period is 0 -> 1 -> 0 -> 1, explain the output sequence. What happens when the clock becomes LOW?", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L110"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q23_compare_a_d_latch_and_a_positive_edge_triggered_d_flip_flop_for_the_same_changing_input_signal_explain_why_the_two_devices_can_produce_different_outputs", "label": "Q23. Compare a D latch and a positive-edge-triggered D flip-flop for the same changing input signal. Explain why the two devices can produce different outputs.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L115"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q24_construct_a_t_flip_flop_using_a_d_flip_flop_and_logic_derive_the_required_d_input_equation", "label": "Q24. Construct a T flip-flop using a D flip-flop and logic. Derive the required D input equation.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L120"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q25_a_jk_flip_flop_is_to_be_implemented_using_a_d_flip_flop_derive_the_expression_for_d_in_terms_of_j_k_and_q", "label": "Q25. A JK flip-flop is to be implemented using a D flip-flop. Derive the expression for D in terms of J, K and Q.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L125"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q26_explain_the_operation_of_an_n_bit_register_why_are_multiple_flip_flops_required", "label": "Q26. Explain the operation of an N-bit register. Why are multiple flip-flops required?", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L130"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q27_a_processor_register_should_load_new_data_only_when_enable_is_high_when_enable_is_low_it_must_retain_its_previous_value_even_when_clock_edges_occur_explain_how_an_enabled_flip_flop_achieves_this_requirement", "label": "Q27. A processor register should load new data only when ENABLE is HIGH. When ENABLE is LOW, it must retain its previous value even when clock edges occur. Explain how an enabled flip-flop achieves this requirement.", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "resources/DLCD_Unit_1_Question_Bank.md", "source_location": "L135"}, {"id": "$graphify-root$_resources_dlcd_unit_1_question_bank_q28_a_digital_system_requires_a_flip_flop_to_return_to_a_known_state_whenever_reset_is_asserted_explain_the_purpose_of_a_resettable_flip_flop_and_distinguish_between_resetting_the_state_and_loading_normal_data", "label": "Q28. A digital system requires a flip-flop t